**1. Overview of Current Terminal Operations**  
**Discussion Points:**  
- Mark Thompson opened the meeting with a presentation on the current status of terminal operations at Seattle Port. He highlighted that terminal throughput has increased by 15% year-over-year, reaching an average of 20,000 TEUs (Twenty-foot Equivalent Units) processed per week in Q1 2024.  
- Mark emphasized the need for increased coordination among terminal staff and shipping companies to handle the anticipated surge in cargo volume projected for Q2 2024 due to upcoming trade agreements.  

**Action Items:**  
- Mark to distribute a detailed report on terminal throughput statistics by March 20, 2024.  
- Mark to coordinate a follow-up meeting with key stakeholders from Oceanic Shipping Co. and Maritime Logistics Inc. to discuss operational improvements by March 30, 2024.  

